Interesting analysis.

> Only the human has the capacity to reach 18/99 and 18 in all stats.
> Thus, I find that I really do prefer the human over any other
> available race. It starts off weaker than the others, but the
> weaknesses fade over time and the strengths come out.

> Is that other people's experience as well? or is there a particular
> race you have come to prefer?

I tend not to look at it that way. Except I go by my personal prejudice;  
I don't like orcs, dwarves, gnomes, and the elves aren't those I'd like,  
from a story character point of view. What that leaves is plain old  
humans.

I've played the other races where they seemed fitting, or to have them  
played at least once, and I do look at the stats and abilities, but to  
be more effective in surmounting my story-mind's prejudices they would  
have to be more diverse. +2 Int and Wiz, for example, isn't enough to  
make the Nethack Elf fit into the same picture that I have of Wizard, so  
I simply dislike that combination.

(In Crawl, while not completely free of my dislike of not only certain  
races, but also fighter types, I took long looks at the skill  
developemnt abilities and other specific stats of each race when  
deciding on a new combination to try. Humans there were more on the  
uninteresting side.)

